WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.200
Two places.

2
00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:05.140
Venice: a bridge, a quay, a courtroom.

3
00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:09.210
Belmont: a garden at
night, lit by candles.

4
00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.750
By the last act, three
couples are married,

5
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.430
and the ships are safe.

6
00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.920
Everyone's happy.

7
00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:18.580
But back in Venice, one man
walks out of the courtroom.

8
00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:20.560
He never reaches Belmont.

9
00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:23.050
Three weddings, a happy ending.

10
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.950
So why do many audiences not laugh?

11
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.230
In this mission, you'll
map two worlds: Venice,

12
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:33.550
of trade and law, and
Belmont, of love and riddles.

13
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.350
You'll follow four plots:
a bond, three caskets,

14
00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.440
an elopement, and a ring.

15
00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:42.760
And you'll test the play
against the rules of comedy.

16
00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:46.940
Your mission: work out why so
many audiences don't laugh.
